From: Mihawk <163614687+mihawk-99@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 14:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] server: a directory reparse tag may be set on a directory that holds files.

FSCTL_SET_REPARSE_POINT refused every directory that held a file with STATUS_DIRECTORY_NOT_EMPTY. Windows 10 1607 and
later accept a tag with the directory bit (IsReparseTagDirectory) there and refuse the others: ntdll file.c:6694
expects the first and 6655 the second. On the console 6694 failed in both builds (2026-10-26, B13). The PC's Wine
passes it by accident: is_dir_empty() reads a dup() of the directory's descriptor, which shares its offset, so after
6655's call has read the directory a later call on the same handle starts at its end and finds it empty (a host test
of the function: first call 0, second 1, the file still there); the console's libc reads it again from the start. A
tag with the directory bit is now accepted on a directory that is not empty, as on Windows.
---
diff --git a/server/fd.c b/server/fd.c
index 20d5991..27eb726 100644
--- a/server/fd.c
+++ b/server/fd.c
@@ -2762,7 +2762,10 @@ static void set_reparse_point( struct fd *fd, struct async *async )
         return;
     }
 
-    if (S_ISDIR(st.st_mode) && !is_dir_empty( fd->unix_fd ))
+    /* a tag with the directory bit may be set on a directory that holds files, as on Windows 10 1607 and later
+     * (ntdll file.c:6694; the PC's Wine passes it only because is_dir_empty's dup() shares the descriptor's offset) */
+    if (S_ISDIR(st.st_mode) && !(get_req_data_size() >= sizeof(ULONG) && IsReparseTagDirectory( *(const ULONG *)get_req_data() )) &&
+        !is_dir_empty( fd->unix_fd ))
     {
         set_error( STATUS_DIRECTORY_NOT_EMPTY );
         return;
